You were more likely just using a weapon that did no bonus damage (like
trying to tickle energy vortices with Mojo). Monster AC is basically
irrelevant; after the early game you hit all monsters 100% of the time,
and monsters get no damage reduction from AC. A player-monster gets:

            mtmp->m_lev = (special ? rn1(16,15) : rnd(16));
            mtmp->mhp = mtmp->mhpmax = d((int)mtmp->m_lev,10) +
                                        (special ? (30 + rnd(30)) : 30);

so ("special" is set in the endgame) d16+14 hit dice, to a maximum of 30,
and (hit-dice)d10 + d30 + 30 hitpoints to an absolute maximum of 360.
Hence a very lucky player-monster can simply have a very large number of
hitpoints.
